  "finalText": "Done. Here's a summary of the changes:\n\n### Problem\nThe `validationResult` check lived **inside the route handler** (`taskRoutes.ts:97-101`), meaning the handler was always invoked even when validation failed — validation was \"too late.\"\n\n### Fix (`src/routes/taskRoutes.ts`)\n1. **Added `handleValidationErrors` middleware** (line 10-17) — a proper Express middleware that checks `validationResult(req)` and short-circuits with 400 + error array before the handler runs.\n2. **Appended it to `createTaskValidation`** (line 26) — so it runs as the last step of validation, before the handler is ever called.\n3. **Removed the inline `validationResult` check** from the `POST /` handler (was lines 97-101) — no longer needed.\n\n### Tests (`tests/taskRoutes.test.ts` — new file)\n- `should reject empty title with 400` — sends `title: \"\"`\n- `should reject missing title with 400` — omits `title` entirely\n- `should reject whitespace-only title with 400` — sends `title: \"   \"`\n- `should create a task with valid title` — sends valid title, expects 201\n\nAll 4 tests pass. The 2 pre-existing failures (`date.test.ts`, `modules.test.ts`) are unrelated.",
